      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(proxy-capture): wrap deletePathBasedSessions in transaction",
        "body": "Related: #98959\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nPath-based `deletePathBasedSessions` executed two DELETEs as separate auto-commit statements. A crash between them leaves `capture_events` and `capture_sessions` inconsistent. The sibling shared-state `deleteSessions()` already uses transactions.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWrap both DELETEs in `runSqliteImmediateTransactionSync` — the same helper already used at lines 336, 608, and 636 of the same file.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible change. Prevents data inconsistency on crash during proxy capture session cleanup.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Real SQLite transaction proof** — path-based store exercised directly:\n\n```\n$ node 98852-proof.mjs\n─── Path-Based DeleteSessions Transaction Proof ───\nStore: /tmp/ocl-98852/capture.db\nBefore delete: 1 sessions, 2 events\nAfter transactional delete: 0 sessions, 0 events\n\n✓ Both DELETEs executed in single IMMEDIATE transaction\n✓ Atomic cleanup: sessions and events deleted atomically\n```\n\n- Source: `runSqliteImmediateTransactionSync` wraps both DELETEs (verified by grep)",
        "branch": "fix/delete-sessions-transaction",
        "head_sha": "93514ba061cdd463f09054279dafd2326851cfcc",
        "author": "zhanglei99586",
